## Workflow-level result + summary (API UI)

Heavy-HTTP tasks that skip inputs via **`_waf_precheck_gate`** still attach per-step **`waf_status`** on step status blobs (existing). The runner also aggregates **`task_executor._step_waf_status`** before final **`POST …/executions/{id}/logs`**:

- **`result`**: **`cancelled_waf`** when any step had all targets blocked on every worker (**fully skipped**); **`partial_waf`** when there were skips but every affected step ran on at least some surviving targets. **`failed`** / **`stopped`** are unchanged; **`waf_summary`** may still be present for operators.
- **`waf_summary`** (JSON): `any_skips`, `fully_skipped_steps`, `partial_skip_steps` (each with `step`, `skipped_inputs`, blocked keys list, `candidate_nodes`), `total_skipped_inputs`, `total_blocked_target_keys`, `candidate_nodes_union`. Stored on **`workflow_logs.waf_summary`**.

## Operational env (runner pod unless noted)

- **`WAF_DETECTION`** — `off` / `false` / `0` / `no` disables gate + secondary signals.
- **`WAF_QUARANTINE_TTL`** — block key TTL seconds (default 1800).
- **`WAF_SECONDARY_PROMOTE`** / **`WAF_SECONDARY_WINDOW`** — promote weak heavy-task signals after N hits in window.
- **`WAF_NODE_LABEL`** — Kubernetes node label key for affinity exclusions (default `kubernetes.io/hostname`).

## Precheck batching / affinity

Heavy HTTP steps invoke **`task_executor._waf_precheck_gate`**: probes are collapsed so each labeled worker gets **one** Job whose command runs nuclei with **multiple lines on stdin** (one URL per probe). Outputs are **`classify_precheck_per_target`**: canonical keys from **`matched-at`** map to **`mark_probed` / `record_blocked`**. Scheduling uses **`job_params["required_nodes"]=[hostname]`**; see **`KubernetesService.generate_job_crd`** (affinity `In` + optional `NotIn` for heavy tasks).

## Extending matchers (precheck)

Precheck nuclei loads only **`waf-precheck-unified.yaml`** (`services/waf_detection.WAF_PRECHECK_TEMPLATE_PATH`): one **`GET`** to `{{RootURL}}` with **`matchers-condition: or`** over every branch mirrored from per-vendor files. To add a detector: extend **`waf-precheck-unified.yaml`** with a new OR matcher **and** add or refresh a **`id: vendor-*`** YAML alongside it as reference/documentation. Matches are counted when nuclei JSONL has **`template-id: waf-precheck-unified`** or the template path contains **`waf-precheck-unified`**; **`vendor`** in the inferred verdict stays **`None`**. Prefer **status + body/header** signals so CDN branding alone does not imply blocked egress.

## Do not

- Put WAF templates only under `src/runner/` — nuclei runs in the **worker** container.
- Key reputation at apex-only — use `target_key()` (scheme + host + port).
